    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear core of elite producers, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill**, who boast scores of 81.88 and 75.27, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** stands out as the day\u2019s premier play, benefitting significantly from a favorable 4.70 xERA matchup against Rea and a massive +16% park adjustment that makes him our primary engine for power and speed. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** is positioned for a high-efficiency outing against Cabrera; despite a minor park penalty, his elite skill projection against the starter creates a strong ceiling. We also see high value in **Kyle Tucker** (75.04) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against high-xERA arms, allowing us to maximize our total base production in the face of our 5x5 Roto constraints.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's lineup card involved the fringe utility slots, where **Brayan Rocchio** (51.40) narrowly missed the cut. While **Brayan Rocchio** offered a respectable floor against Prielipp, the optimizer prioritized the aggressive platoon and order advantages held by **Curtis Mead** (61.43) and **Miguel Vargas** (53.76). **Miguel Vargas** remains a strategic hold due to his elite xwOBA (.406) and a boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a unique efficiency edge for our stolen base objectives. Conversely, we must exercise caution with **Heliot Ramos** (43.02) and **Josh Lowe** (41.60); **Heliot Ramos** faces a formidable challenge against Cease, and **Josh Lowe** is suppressed by a negative platoon shift and a bottom-of-the-order assignment, making both high-risk starts despite their baseline potential. \n\nRegarding roster health, we continue to monitor the absence of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains on the IL. We are currently navigating these daily caps by keeping depth options like **Denzer Guzman** and **Jorge Polanco** on the bench, ensuring we only deploy players like **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin** when their platoon splits dictate a scoring advantage. We are keeping a close watch on potential lineup volatility; any late-scratch news would force us to re-evaluate our pinch-hit contingency plan, but for now, the data suggests prioritizing the power-speed combination of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker** to maintain our competitive edge in the standings.",
